{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220161-elohim-s-blood","id":1220161,"title":"Elohim's Blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-18T19:52:37-07:00","id":1220161,"title":"Elohim's Blood","content":"So. i been thinking and pondering a lot about Angels and Demons on the lore of the World of Darkness..<br /> and i came up with some theories about Elohim's biology. <br /> <br /> So my theories are as such. The DNA/Blood and any other biological functions of the Host are escensially normal. But once the Host is forced to change his Visage/Expose itself or reveal his true nature (by showing his wings etc..) Part of his biology or more like genetical makeup changes slightly. forcing the body to adapt to the new changes within the host body structure.<br /> <br /> What i been exploring is the following idea for a scenario im currently running. a NPC was captured and was tortured for days but forcing him to maintain part of his Demonic Self. The blood related to the area of this Exposure tends to differ from the rest. as if was made by a &quot;Parasitic&quot; organism (if we were to use something similiar for this effect). Hence. the blood from the shoulder is completely different from the blood from the wings or near the horns.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right now im doing a system in which if anyone injects the proper demon blood, he would have a couple of apocalyptic forms but depending on the torment level, the person who injects himself would be driven completely mad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T21:11:38-07:00","id":1220180,"title":"","content":"Why would the blood remain the same after the Demon goes back to normal human form? Just because it was removed from the body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T02:13:56-07:00","id":1220207,"title":"","content":"Injection of demon blood to gain some of their powers are nice. I'd keep it on a level, where the user would gain maybe one power of the apocalypse form, plus a torment power if the blood was taken from either a high torment demon or an unwilling target. I don't really like the &quot;the blood here is totally different from the blood over there&quot; thing, as the blood is circulating through the entire body, thus it's pretty much the same all over the organism. Maybe just use the most manifested/most basic ability the demon can manifest.<br /> <br /> For DNA, in a technological setting, your explanation might be necessary, but the act of &quot;cannibalizing&quot; a demons essence/blood works pretty well in a mystical sense, too. (Sorry, if I get a bit Mage-y over here). I don't know what setting you're running, so I guess a scientific explanation is good to have, but in case the PCs are not real scientists I'd prefer a more mystical approach, as only a technocratic Agent could maintain a strictly scientific world view when dealing with demons, angels, vampires and such. But of course that's up to you.<br /> <br /> For Torment-affliction, how does the madness progress? Is it derangements that get worse the more demon blood is used? Or more like an approach, where the user's mind gets subtly invaded by the demons Torment and he goes up the scale, as a demon would. In the latter case, at a certain point, every injection could trigger torment-powers to manifest in the user, as his/her own Torment-rating would be high enough to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T04:14:22-07:00","id":1220226,"title":"","content":"I could see adding an &quot;addiction&quot; flaw to it on top of the risk of madness/derangement. The rush of the power could be quite addictive despite the nasty side effect of he Torment, Hell not the first drug to have a nasty down. <br /> <br /> So they would try to get more and more and more. Maybe even becoming thrall or a hunter for steady(er) fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T16:47:24-07:00","id":1220366,"title":"","content":"ok purpouses of this?<br /> <br /> Im using it on my MtAs game as a drug made by nephandi (which they want to use in hospitals for blood transfusion and cause chaos). the purpouse is nto only regenerative, but also highly addictive. it gives you the Madness derangement from 1 - 10 but based on the permanent torment of the demon minus the willpower of the human who uses it. the result would be the level of the derangement.<br /> <br /> basically, the person who uses the demon blood becomes a psycho for a couple of hours but is still tempted to compel to his darkest desires. <br /> <br /> as for the demon blood itself, i been thinking (OK TRIGGER WARNING HERE) on how nephandi could use it. like forcing a demon to stay on his proper revelatory form..and rape it in order to produce a Nephilim of some sorts. or to at least hope that a human will attempt to create an artificial monster","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}